== 1.1 Health and Its Dimensions

The World Health Organization's constitutional definition describes health as a state of physical, mental and social wellbeing, not merely the absence of disease or infirmity. It is a broad ideal; real experiences vary over time, and a person living with a condition can still pursue wellbeing and participate meaningfully in community life.

*Physical health* concerns the functioning and condition of the body. *Mental wellbeing* includes emotional and psychological experiences and the ability to cope and seek support. *Social wellbeing* concerns relationships, belonging and participation. These dimensions interact: an injury may affect activity, mood and social participation, while supportive relationships can help a person's recovery. None can be reliably measured by appearance alone.

#rule-box("Health is multidimensional")[
  Distinguish a definition from an individual diagnosis. One symptom, body size or test result does not reveal everything about a person's health. A qualified professional can assess a specific concern in context.
]

== 1.2 Personal Hygiene

Personal hygiene means practices that help keep the body clean and reduce certain health risks. Hand hygiene is especially important before preparing or eating food, after using the toilet, and after contact with potentially contaminated material. Wash hands with soap and clean running water, rubbing all surfaces and drying them. If soap and water are unavailable, an alcohol-based hand rub containing at least 60% alcohol can be used; it is less effective on visibly dirty or greasy hands, and soap and water are preferred where available.

Bathing, clean clothing, safe menstrual materials and regular oral care can support comfort and health. Brush teeth with fluoride toothpaste and seek dental advice as needed. Menstrual hygiene should be addressed without shame: clean materials, privacy, safe disposal and access to water all matter. Hygiene practices do not guarantee that a person will never become ill, and lack of water or safe facilities may restrict the choices available.

